# Pinned `spec` revision the conformance runner validates against.
#
# The runner refuses to run if the spec checkout it is given is not at this
# commit (override with --allow-spec-drift when deliberately testing against
# unreleased vocabulary). Without a pin the suite silently tracks whatever is
# on spec `main`, so a run that passed yesterday can pass today for a
# different reason.
#
# To re-pin: check out the new spec revision, put its full SHA and its
# VOCAB_VERSIONS line below, run `make -C . conformance` (or
# `scripts/run_conformance.py`), and record the resulting counts in the PR.

# This pin is the MERGE commit of the-cascade-protocol/spec PR #48 on `main`
# (core v3.8 / health v2.9 / clinical v1.18 / coverage v1.6). It replaces the
# DRAFT pin this conformance PR opened with, 0d07ade, the head of the spec
# branch feat/health-2.9-coded-allergy, which was a commit a fresh clone of spec
# could not resolve. That branch has since merged. The two trees are
# byte-identical -- `git diff 0d07ade 0bdfe09` is empty -- so the counts below
# were re-measured rather than carried over, and came back unchanged against a
# revision that is now reachable from `main`.
#
# TAGS NOT YET PUSHED: `vocab/health-v2.9` and `vocab/clinical-v1.18` do not
# exist on the spec remote as of this commit. `git ls-remote --tags` names
# `vocab/health-v2.8` and `vocab/clinical-v1.17` as the newest of each, both on
# earlier commits. The pin resolves a SHA and depends on no tag, so nothing in
# this suite is affected; recorded so a reader who goes looking for those tags
# knows they are absent rather than mistyped.
#
# Previously pinned on `main` at 9b13ae4, the MERGE commit of
# the-cascade-protocol/spec PR #32 (core v3.8 / health v2.8 / clinical v1.17 /
# coverage v1.6; tags `vocab/core-v3.8`, `vocab/clinical-v1.17`,
# `vocab/coverage-v1.6` point at that commit; `vocab/health-v2.8` remains on the
# pin before it).
#
# WHAT MOVING THE PIN DID, measured with this branch's fixture set against both
# revisions: 137 passed / 30 failed / 0 skipped / 167 total and 63,447
# constraint checks at 9b13ae4, becoming 140 / 27 / 0 / 167 and 63,543 here.
# (The 9b13ae4 figure is a `--allow-spec-drift` run against a checkout of that
# commit, which is what the flag is for. It is not ratcheted and is not the
# suite's result; the suite's result is the second pair.)
#
# Exactly three verdicts changed and all three are fixtures this PR adds:
# health/coded-allergy-allergen-code-string.WARN, -criticality-moderate.WARN and
# -type-sensitivity.WARN each report NO_WARNING at 9b13ae4 -- nothing notices
# them, because none of the four constraints exists there -- and pass here. The
# fourth new fixture, health/coded-allergy-penicillin.VALID, passes at BOTH
# revisions; the release is strictly widening, so passing is not what proves it.
# What proves it is the constraint check count. All twelve fixtures that
# instantiate health:AllergyRecord go 28 -> 36 checks -- the six
# allergy-00*.json, health/status-allergy-inactive.VALID,
# health/status-allergy-entered-in-error.WARN and the four new ones -- which is
# the four new property shapes on health:AllergyRecordShape actually evaluating,
# and which accounts for the whole +96. No pre-existing fixture changes verdict
# or reason, which is the release's "additive and strictly widening" claim
# measured rather than quoted.
#
# WHAT MOVING TO 9b13ae4 DID, one pin earlier: exactly one verdict changed, and
# it is the one that pin's baseline predicted. clinical/status-laboratoryreport-
# in-progress.WARN.ttl -- baselined before it as a spec-owned defect (sh:node
# escalating nested sh:Warning to sh:Violation on the six document subtypes) --
# started passing: clinical v1.17 moved the two Warning bindings onto
# target-class shapes (DocumentStatusShape, DocumentReferenceStatusShape), so
# the warning fires named and nothing else does. Its KNOWN_FAILURES entry was
# removed in the same commit, per the ratchet. core v3.8 defines
# cascade:PatientReported, the provenance individual seventeen shapes already
# accepted; coverage v1.6 adds cascade:AIExtracted to InsurancePlanShape's
# dataProvenance set. Neither changed any existing fixture's verdict; the
# AIExtracted InsurancePlan and documentReferenceStatus WARN fixtures that
# release makes possible are tracked upstream rather than rushed here.
#
# Re-measured at this commit: 140 passed / 27 failed / 0 skipped / 167 total,
# 63,543 constraint checks. All 27 are enumerated in KNOWN_FAILURES.json, whose
# specPin is advanced to this same SHA in this commit, so the ratchet holds.

